# Fear of Burning Alive: "When this creature enters, it deals 4 damage to each opponent." and "Delirium - Whenever a source you
# control deals noncombat damage to an opponent, if there are four or more card types among cards in your graveyard, this creature
# deals that amount of damage to target creature that player controls." Turn 1: Bot1 casts three Moxen, then Black Lotus pays for
# Wheel of Fortune, which puts Black Lotus (artifact), the Wheel (sorcery), an Ornithopter (artifact creature) and an Island (land)
# into Bot1's graveyard: exactly four types (CR 207.2c). The Wheel makes Bot2 discard and draw seven too. Turn 2 Bot2 casts an
# Aegis Turtle (0/5). Turn 3 Bot1 casts Fear with six mana: its own enters trigger deals 4 to Bot2 (a source Bot1 controls), the
# delirium ability triggers (Bot2's Turtle is the one creature it can target) and the Turtle is dealt exactly 4. Turn 4 Bot2's own
# Lightning Bolt to its own face (a source Bot2 controls, not Bot1) does not trigger it. Bot2 then casts a Steel Wall (0/4). Turn 5
# Bot1's Bolt to its own face (not an opponent) does not trigger it; a Bolt to Bot2's face (3 noncombat damage by a spell Bot1
# controls, CR 120.2b) does: Bot1's own Fear is refused as a target and the Steel Wall is dealt exactly 3, the Turtle healed.

